            <p><strong>2. Run the installer.</strong> Double-click AZERTY_Global.exe, make sure
            “Add to language bar list” is checked, then click “Install”.</p>
            <p><strong>3. Check that it’s active.</strong> Click <strong>FRA</strong> in the taskbar:
            if “AZERTY Global” appears, select it. If it doesn’t appear,
            add it through Settings → Time &amp; language → Language &amp; region → French (…) → Language
            options → Add a keyboard. If nothing happens, restart the computer and try again.</p>
            <p><strong>4. Switch keyboards</strong> with <span class="insecable"><kbd>Win</kbd> + <kbd>Space</kbd></span>, or by
            clicking <strong>FRA</strong> in the taskbar.</p>
            <p><strong>Keep AZERTY Global as the default:</strong> remove the old keyboards you no longer
            need (Settings → Time &amp; language → Language &amp; region → French (…) → Language options →
            Keyboards), or set AZERTY Global as the default input method in
            Settings → Time &amp; language → Typing → Advanced keyboard settings →
            “Override for default input method”.</p>
            <p><strong>Check:</strong> press the key marked <kbd>;</kbd>. It should type a period. <a href="/en/guide">One-keystroke check in the guide</a>.</p>
