        <div class="canaux">
          <article class="canal">
            <h3>macOS installer</h3>
            <p class="canal__contexte">macOS 10.12 or later. A .keylayout file to install manually.</p>
            <a href="https://sourceforge.net/projects/azertyglobal/files/AZERTY_Global_macOS.zip/download"
              id="btn-download-macos"
              class="bouton bouton--primaire">Download for macOS</a>
            <details class="notice">
              <summary>Installation instructions</summary>
              <div class="notice__contenu prose">
                <p><strong>1. Open the Finder.</strong> In the “Go” menu, hold down the
                <kbd>Option</kbd> (Alt) key, then click “Library”.</p>
                <p><strong>2. Open the Keyboard Layouts folder</strong> (create it if it doesn’t exist).
                Full path: <code>~/Library/Keyboard Layouts/</code></p>
                <p><strong>3. Copy the file AZERTY Global.keylayout</strong> into that folder. For all
                users: <code>/Library/Keyboard Layouts/</code> (administrator password
                required).</p>
                <p><strong>4. Log out and back in.</strong> This is required for macOS to detect the
                file.</p>
                <p><strong>5. Add the keyboard:</strong> System Settings → Keyboard → Text Input →
                Edit… → “+” → look under “Others” or
                “French” → AZERTY Global → Add (before macOS 13: System
                Preferences → Keyboard → Input Sources).</p>
                <p><strong>Usage:</strong> click the keyboard icon in the menu bar
                and select AZERTY Global. Switch between keyboards with
                <kbd>Ctrl</kbd> + <kbd>Space</kbd> (or <kbd>Cmd</kbd> + <kbd>Space</kbd> depending on your
                settings).</p>
                <p><strong>Check:</strong> press the key marked <kbd>;</kbd>. It should type a period. <a href="/en/guide">One-keystroke check in the guide</a>.</p>
              </div>
            </details>
            <details class="notice">
              <summary>Uninstall</summary>
              <div class="notice__contenu prose">
                <p>System Settings → Keyboard → Text Input → select AZERTY Global →
                “−” (before macOS 13: System Preferences → Keyboard → Input
                Sources). Then delete the file <code>AZERTY Global.keylayout</code> from
                <code>~/Library/Keyboard Layouts/</code>, and log out and back in.</p>
              </div>
            </details>
          </article>
        </div>
