                <p><code>chmod +x install.sh</code><br><code>sudo ./install.sh</code></p>
                <p><strong>3. Log out and back in</strong>, or restart.</p>
                <p><strong>4. Add the keyboard.</strong> GNOME / Fedora / Ubuntu: Settings →
                Keyboard → Input Sources → “+” → three dots at the bottom of the list → type
                “azerty global” → “Other” → French (AZERTY Global).
                KDE / Plasma: System Settings → Keyboard → Layouts → Add →
                French (AZERTY Global).</p>
                <p><strong>Check:</strong> press the key marked <kbd>;</kbd>. It should type a period. <a href="/en/guide">One-keystroke check in the guide</a>.</p>
              </div>
            </details>
            <details class="notice">
              <summary>Uninstall</summary>
              <div class="notice__contenu prose">
                <p>Remove AZERTY Global from your input sources, then delete the layout file
                with <code>sudo rm /usr/share/X11/xkb/symbols/azerty_global</code>. If
                needed, restore your previous <code>~/.XCompose</code>: the installation backed it up
                as <code>~/.XCompose.backup.</code> followed by the date and time. Then log out
                and back in.</p>
              </div>
            </details>
